  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "As [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) begins, you can pick one of the 3 combat doctrines below. Your **ADEPTUS ASTARTES** units that have this ability then benefit from it until your next Command phase. The doctrines are:\n\n- **Assault Doctrine**: the unit can still declare a charge after making an **[advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move)**.\n- **Devastator Doctrine**: the unit's ranged attacks get **[[ASSAULT]](vsdata:weapon-ability/assault)**.\n- **Tactical Doctrine**: the unit can still shoot and declare a charge after making a **[fall-back move](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back)**.\n\nUnless a rule says otherwise:\n\n- You can pick each combat doctrine only once per battle.\n- A unit can have just one combat doctrine active at a time. If a rule makes another one active for it, the doctrine it had before stops being active.",
